invariant: INV-26
file: src/record.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh x86-kernels
reason: the record layer's open builds its AES key and never records the
  direction's cpu in it, so every record it opens under AES-GCM runs
  gcm_hw.c's 128-bit loops, whatever CH_CPU_VAES says. The bytes are the
  same.
  bin/x86_kernels_test counts the calls into each kernel under every
  ch_cfg.cpu value, and test/aes-runtime-qemu.sh builds it for x86-64 and
  runs it under qemu-x86_64. The lane skips without docker, and this then
  reports unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
    aes_traffic_gcm_key_of(&k, d->cpu, d);
    int ok = gcm_traffic_open(&k, nonce, rec, REC_HDR, rec + REC_HDR, len, rec + REC_HDR + len, pt);
--- new
    aes_traffic_gcm_key_of(&k, 0, d);
    int ok = gcm_traffic_open(&k, nonce, rec, REC_HDR, rec + REC_HDR, len, rec + REC_HDR + len, pt);
